Refactor one bounded FLEXT behavior at a time. Runtime reality and the real consumer decide correctness; tests and static gates only confirm the proven contract.

Read, in order:

1. [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)
2. [FLEXT Context Routing](../../.agents/skills/flext-context-routing/SKILL.md)
3. The path-specific rule or skill for the files being changed

Execute in this order:

1. Claim the Bead and preserve the current user intent and useful WIP.
2. Establish expected behavior from the official external contract and observe it with the real consumer.
3. Search canonical FLEXT facades, services, models, protocols, settings, generators, and current callers.
4. Improve the existing lowest stable owner. Never create a competing helper, engine, parser, executor, alias, config route, or type carrier.
5. Validate untrusted input once into the owning typed model. Reuse that object internally; serialize only at external egress.
6. Migrate every consumer in the same slice. Delete old paths, wrappers, fallbacks, shims, compatibility behavior, duplicated constants, and dict/model round-trips.
7. Exercise the real public surface again. Fix forward until the consumer accepts the result.
8. Only then run the config-owned local workflow, in order:
{% for step in make.workflow if "local" in step.contexts %}
   - `make {{ step.verb }}{% if step.apply %} {{ make.apply_variable }}={{ make.apply_value }}{% endif %}`
{% endfor %}
9. Fix every failure at its canonical owner and replay from the invalidated stage.

Use canonical root facades and MRO composition. Prefer the project’s established `c`, `m`, `p`, `t`, `u`, `r`, and service surfaces over direct framework imports or local reinvention. Search before adding any symbol. Add a contract only when no existing owner can be improved.

Never invoke Ruff, Pyrefly, Pyright, Mypy, Pytest, formatters, generators, or dependency tools directly. Their owning Make verb controls scope, order, serialization, and evidence. `make conform` is read-only and separate from generation; it does not run in CI or pre-commit and never accepts APPLY.

Finish the slice only when all affected runtime consumers, generated artifacts, tests, static gates, docs, repository state, commit, push, and Bead evidence agree. A partial migration or locally green subset is not complete.
